                DescribeRole.Theorem),
            Describe.Lean(DescribeId.Create("realinfimumprimeboundary-real-infimum-fixed-price-squeeze"),
                DeclarationHandle.Create(Prefix + "real_infimum_fixed_price_squeeze"),
                H("Uniform finite bound on the actual sInf"),
                StatementSource.WithoutFormula(), AssessedProvenance.FromRepo(),
                Blocks(Paragraph(Text("For card S>=3, ell=log H>=1 and any r>0, set A=exp(ell*(exp r-1))-1. The proof works pointwise on each original admissible real vector x. Put T=clock S x and u=(T-H)/H>=0. The exact benefit-log identity gives phi(x)-baseline=F(T)-F(H)+U(x), with U(x)>=0. The nested-log identity and two applications of the pinned elementary log bound give F(T)-F(H)>=u/ell-u^2/ell. Summing boundary_maximum and using the canonical sum_price identity gives Q-u^2/ell<=phi(x)-baseline. If this gap is below r, invert both positive logarithms to obtain u<A; otherwise r already bounds it. Thus min(r,Q-A^2/ell) bounds every original value gap. Applying le_csInf to the same nonempty realValues proves the lower bound. The feasible boundary vector and real_infimum_bounds give realInfimum<=phi(b). Nonnegative tangentRemainder then gives realInfimum-baseline<=Q. All conditional-completeness premises come from the literal nonempty and bounded-below value set, with no attained optimizer, stationarity or RH premise."))),
                DescribeRole.Theorem),
